  "reason": "Evidence: Among RNA encoders, scvi_n200 is the clear winner (acc 0.520, F1 0.498) over pca_n2000 (0.485) and scgpt (0.411), and image-only resnet50 is very weak (0.208), indicating RNA dominates. All four completed experiments are singleprofile, so the effect of multiprofile is entirely untested. Question: Does multiprofile with simple avgpool aggregation improve upon singleprofile when paired with the best RNA encoder (scvi_n200)? This directly compares to config_004 (same encoder, singleprofile), isolating the profile-setting/aggregation effect. Why this is the best next experiment: It builds on the strongest evidence (scvi_n200), tests the single most important unexplored design axis (multiprofile vs singleprofile), and uses the simplest aggregation (avgpool) to avoid confounding. If multiprofile+avgpool helps, it justifies investing in transformer aggregation and multimodal fusion; if it doesn't, it saves budget by ruling out an entire branch of configurations before committing to more complex multimodal setups."
